Fish: events of the blocks Fish mods register, from the block simulation (P8.2).

Horizon runs a block's neighbour updates, scheduled ticks and random ticks in `Sim`, a generic
type (`impl<L: LevelAccess + ?Sized> Sim<'_, L>`) that horizon-mixins cannot hook. This patch adds
one call at the start of `neighbor_changed`, `tick_block` and `random_tick_block`; it asks
`fish_hooks` whether the state is one of a block a mod registered (a comparison with the
loader's state ranges) and then raises the block event with no game view: the role and the
dimension are what the game thread last noted (`fish_hooks::note_thread_context`). Horizon's
`neighbor_changed` names the block that changed, not its position, so the event's neighbour
position is the block's own. The patch adds `fish-hooks` to horizon-world (`horizon/cargo-edits.toml`).

diff --git a/crates/horizon-world/src/level/hooks.rs b/crates/horizon-world/src/level/hooks.rs
index f402e8e..2ba57e4 100644
--- a/crates/horizon-world/src/level/hooks.rs
+++ b/crates/horizon-world/src/level/hooks.rs
@@ -18,6 +18,8 @@ impl<L: LevelAccess + ?Sized> Sim<'_, L> {
         changed: BlockId,
         moved: bool,
     ) {
+        // Fish: a block a mod registered hears about its neighbours.
+        fish_block_event(fish_hooks::BlockEventKind::NeighborChanged, state, pos);
         let b = self.b;
         let block = b.block(state);
         let chain = &b.data(state).chain;
@@ -663,3 +665,21 @@ impl super::Behaviours {
         self.props.sculk_sensor_phase
     }
 }
+
+/// Fish: tells the block a mod registered (when `state` is one) that `kind` happened to it.
+/// Horizon names the block that changed for a neighbour change, not where, so `other_pos` is `pos`.
+pub(super) fn fish_block_event(
+    kind: fish_hooks::BlockEventKind,
+    state: BlockStateId,
+    pos: BlockPos,
+) {
+    let Some(d) = fish_hooks::get().filter(|d| d.is_block_state(state.0)) else {
+        return;
+    };
+    let (role, dimension) = fish_hooks::thread_context();
+    let mut event = fish_hooks::BlockEvent::new(kind, state.0, [pos.x, pos.y, pos.z]);
+    event.other_pos = event.pos;
+    event.role = role;
+    event.dimension = dimension;
+    d.block_event(None, &event);
+}
